Another angle is using NaN or values near numerical precision limits—if a race causes even slight deviations, they could accumulate through the exponential operations. The fact that this mutation survived 112 test rounds despite the stress patterns suggests the race either doesn't manifest under typical GPU scheduling, or when it does occur, the values happen to work out correctly anyway. On modern NVIDIA hardware, __syncthreads() likely has specific implementation details that make this particular race hard to trigger. the mutant skips the synchronization, warp 0 might read stale data from warp 7's writes before they're visible. Given the consistent test results across 112 rounds with various stress patterns, the mutant appears functionally equivalent on this particular hardware setup, though it could fail on different GPUs or driver versions.

